                <pb facs="0507" n="393" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg393"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5744: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-11-12T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 12,
                                1924—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 12—3:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following telegram has been received from Nanking: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 11, 5 p.m. Please send following telegram to the Department for
                            me: ‘I have seen Marshal Chi today. He and Admiral Tu have sent vessel
                            to meet Wu who is expected to arrive about the 13th for a conference.
                            Chi has sent circular telegram supporting Tuan. Will accept Tuan’s
                            leadership but not that of Feng or Chang. Invasion by the last two would
                            be forcibly resisted.</p>
                        <p>Representatives of the governors of eight provinces now are assembling
                            here to decide upon course of action. Davis.’”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
